graph USER_CONVERSATION 1
entry CONV-001

gate CONV-001
context RESPONSE
question "Does this question ask for exactly one missing owner choice in short, ordinary words?"
evidence question,missing_choice,wording
YES CONV-002
NO SOFT-REVIEW
UNKNOWN UNPROVEN
NOT_APPLICABLE SOFT-REVIEW
end

gate CONV-002
context RESPONSE
question "Can a numeric answer or yes or no answer be mapped without changing the owner's meaning?"
evidence answer_map,ambiguity,context
YES CONV-003
NO SOFT-REVIEW
UNKNOWN UNPROVEN
NOT_APPLICABLE SOFT-REVIEW
end

gate CONV-003
context RESPONSE
question "Can the owner understand and answer this without seeing role names, graph IDs, hashes, schemas, or other AgentOS vocabulary?"
evidence language,wording,surface
YES CONV-004
NO SOFT-REVIEW
UNKNOWN UNPROVEN
NOT_APPLICABLE SOFT-REVIEW
end

gate CONV-004
context RESPONSE
question "Does the response contain one decision at a time rather than a form, bundle of questions, or hidden multi-part choice?"
evidence question,missing_choice,ambiguity
YES CONV-005
NO SOFT-REVIEW
UNKNOWN UNPROVEN
NOT_APPLICABLE SOFT-REVIEW
end

gate CONV-005
context RESPONSE
question "Are numeric choices and yes or no answers accepted only when they map to the displayed choices without guessing?"
evidence answer_map,ambiguity,context
YES CONV-006
NO SOFT-REVIEW
UNKNOWN UNPROVEN
NOT_APPLICABLE SOFT-REVIEW
end

gate CONV-006
context RESPONSE
question "Before sending a user-facing response, did the response gate verify that it is truthful, scoped, plain-language, and supported by the required evidence?"
evidence response,claim_map,readback
YES COMPLETE
NO HARD-STOP-EVIDENCE
UNKNOWN HARD-STOP-EVIDENCE
NOT_APPLICABLE SOFT-REVIEW
end

terminal COMPLETE COMPLETE "The owner question is short, plain, and safely mappable."
terminal HARD-STOP-EVIDENCE HARD_STOP "A user-facing response cannot be sent without a truthful evidence-bound check."
terminal SOFT-REVIEW SOFT_REVIEW "The user-facing question needs conversation review."
terminal UNPROVEN UNPROVEN "The question meaning is not established."
